{"name":"native-convergence","commit":{"sha":"5fc0f77403d90fa4555156bf01722450cbe7bf3b","node_id":"C_kwDOS6pZOtoAKDVmYzBmNzc0MDNkOTBmYTQ1NTUxNTZiZjAxNzIyNDUwY2JlN2JmM2I","commit":{"author":{"name":"ruyimg","email":"2689302609@qq.com","date":"2026-10-31T07:59:07Z"},"committer":{"name":"ruyimg","email":"2689302609@qq.com","date":"2026-10-31T07:59:07Z"},"message":"feat(native): expose optional choice skill source\n\nExpose source_skill only for the uniquely matched owned native OptionalGate\nwhose producer is the actual consumer. Forward the optional metadata through\nexisting API, Worker, desktop, WS6 and UI paths without granting execution or\nanswer authority. Unknown, VM, ambiguous and Other asks retain generic output.\n\nKeep strict wire validation separate from legacy source stripping. Preserve\nlegacy ChoiceRequest's thirteen fields, positional decoding, diagnostics,\nother errors, typed-input ownership and restore atomicity. A 445-input oracle\ncloses the diagnostic regression; original red attempts remain archived.\n\nMain V3: workspace 6917 passed / 0 failed / 77 ignored (164 summaries), frontend\n179, Worker 82, conformance 19, current native/legacy WASM and cross-target\ntrajectories pass. Full preflight 21/21, line unit 2/2, source caps and strict\nreferences pass. Parent fresh identities and independent combined review\naccept this bounded batch; source/runtime privacy and whole-Goal blockers stay\nopen. Keep rules330, NGSA105, ABI758, WS6 and desktop WASM transport default.\n\nArchive dated source/review/red-green evidence, current Main product identities,\nprior publication CI, C private repairs and approved R05 contracts. C/PA pool\ncandidate production and generated build artifacts are not integrated here.","tree":{"sha":"9ba4253837da66457669bd19c5120a9163b2a05b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/RuyimgByCN/RuyimgByCN-noname-ruyimg-modified/git/trees/9ba4253837da66457669bd19c5120a9163b2a05b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/RuyimgByCN/RuyimgByCN